The DeepWork review came back clean on all three rules, with no findings and no changes made. Two of the passes were weaker than they sound.

- **`no_em_dashes`:** passed. The file has no em dashes.
- **`update_documents_relating_to_archy_package`:** passed. Every #548 figure the doc quotes matches `bench/diff_duplicates_precision_results.md`, and 557 / 1,049 does give 0.531. The reviewer didn't verify `MIN_NODES = 30` because it looked in `src`. The constant is defined at `bench/diff_duplicates_precision.py:52`, so the doc is right.
- **`suggest_new_reviews`:** passed, but the reviewer never opened either file and passed on its default criterion. Treat that as no review.

Your standing rule is to include an adversarial pass, and none of the three rules is one. They check formatting and drift, not whether the design holds up. I haven't run one. I'd aim it at the places where I departed from the ticket:
- the cutoff calibration;
- the (PR, new function) pool unit;
- the "only by B" definition;
- whether the thresholds can be cleared trivially given A's 0.16 precision.

Want me to run it before you merge #965? Edits after merge can only go in as addenda.

